what is going on everybody welcome back  to the cosmic wonder i'm your host  warren thompson and it looks like we  were robbed quite a bit with doctor  strange in the multiverse of madness  recently it has been revealed that they  cut two really really cool scenes from  multiverse of madness one of them  involving another fight between the  scarlet witch and doctor strange and  possibly even more evil variants of  doctor strange but the other deleted  scene involves nightmare one of the most  popular doctor strange villain who we  thought was going to be the main villain  of this movie who was supposed to be the  villain of the first movie but didn't  end up in either of the films although  we did think he was going to be at least  a villain in this movie especially with  the tease of doctor strange saying that  every day he has the same nightmare the  same with wanda it did certainly seem  like they were setting up the villain  nightmare to make at least an appearance  however it looks like in the end they  decided to go with the scarlet witch  being the main villain of the movie but  today we actually have a look at what it  could have been like if nightmare was  indeed in doctor strange in the  multiverse of madness including what is  a deleted scene that was cut from the  movie involving doctor strange nightmare  and his sister who died falling through  the ice that they briefly mentioned at  the end of multiverse of madness now for  those of you who don't know originally  nightmare was supposed to be the main  villain of doctor strange number one  scott derrickson directed the first  movie and they wanted to do nightmare  but they decided to leave it for doctor  strange too and i don't know if some of  you remember this but originally scott  derrickson was supposed to direct doctor  strange 2 and doctor strange 2 was truly  supposed to be the mcu's first horror  film and this is something that scott  derrickson really really wanted to do so  the villain nightmare was really a  perfect fit however due to creative  differences scott derrickson backed out  of the project now from what we  understand the creative differences were  scott derrickson really wanted a true  horror film but kevin foggy of course  said this still needs to be pg-13 we  can't go full rated r we can't do all of  the true horror stuff that you want to  do based off of everything that we've  heard that's what happened so then they  brought in sam raimi and honestly doctor  strange and the multiverse of madness  was still pretty creepy but we didn't  see nightmare in the movie however we  almost did but they cut it out of the  movie but here we have some actual  photos from what would have been in the  movie and some photos of nightmare and  how he would have looked if we saw him  in multiverse of madness now this is set  design here using figures so as you can  see here we have doctor strange standing  on a frozen lake and we have nightmare  standing on a horse in front of him now  we'll go back to this in just a second  but first let's go to this look at  nightmare in the book now this is what  marvel studios labeled this book it says  nightmare character ancient text and  illustrations this is something  apparently labeled as a dream codex and  it shows nightmare in what looks to be  medieval armor riding a horse there's a  lot of drawings also in the background  in the upper left it seems like it could  be the cycles of the moon but we also do  have another page of this dream codex  that looks a little bit different  showing him in different armor this one  looks a lot more cool and it actually  shows him in samurai armor riding more  of a traditional horse and he has four  horns on his head and there's a lot of  text on this book that is really just  too small to make out but here we are  getting our first look at what nightmare  would have looked like in multiverse of  madness but going back to doctor strange  and nightmare being on the frozen lake  here we have actually multiple scales of  the set that they were designing and  here's where we find out what the scene  with nightmare was originally intended  to be in the film before they actually  made the decision to cut it and it does  appear to be a scene on a frozen lake  with dr strange's sister donna strange  now like i said they ultimately did kind  of mention this scene at the end of  doctor strange where he's fighting with  sinister strange doctor strange talks  about the time where he was on the lake  with his sister donna who would go on to  fall through the ice and sadly die now  that happens no matter what however here  it looks like nightmare is sort of  haunting doctor strange and giving him  nightmares about when his sister died  and the fact that doctor strange could  not save her but the coolest thing here  is it actually looks like doctor strange  was going to fight nightmare we see  nightmare on the horse and it looks like  he is wearing the costume and the armor  from the second design the more samurai  looking armor and across from him we see  doctor strange ready to fight so sadly  it looks like we were deprived of a  doctor strange versus nightmare fight  now like i mentioned they originally  teased us with nightmare in the trailers  where we heard doctor strange and wanda  say nightmare so it's probably safe to  assume that they did really intent on  this scene being in the movie but as we  know they cut multiple scenes and doctor  strange in the multiverse of madness was  only a little bit over two hours long it  was relatively short compared to what  we've gotten recently from marvel  studios but perhaps they are saving this  scene for another doctor strange movie  clia has now been introduced into the  mcu we know that incursions are  happening so we know that we are going  to be getting a doctor strange 3 and  even though there's going to be a lot  going on with those incursions and such  they're still going to need a villain  and perhaps nightmare has just been  pushed back to doctor strange 3.  hopefully we get nightmare at some point  in time because in this picture in this  book he does look pretty awesome and now  doctor strange honestly has even more  things to have nightmares about  christine palmer is now married he had  to essentially kill himself even though  it was an evil variant and he had to  watch a lot of sorcerers die at the  hands of wanda so nightmare could  definitely still be used in another film  so fingers crossed that we see him now  there was another scene that was cut  from this movie that involved a fight  between doctor strange america chavez  and the scarlet witch and i think i  would have actually been more interested  in seeing this scene than what we got on  the screen in the movie america chavez  gets scared she opens up a portal and  her and doctor strange go through the  portal no one else the scarlet witch  doesn't go through wang doesn't go  through it is just doctor strange and  america chavez they go through a bunch  of different universes until they  eventually land into the universe where  the illuminati exist and they meet mordo  but sadly we found out that this scene  was originally supposed to be doctor  strange and wanda going at it something  that we didn't actually truly see in  multiverse of madness a one-on-one fight  between doctor strange and wanda now we  did kind of get undead strange fighting  wanda but we didn't get a full-on doctor  strange at his best fighting wanda in  this scene the star portal opens and  strange and the scarlet witch jump in  the portal after america chavez they  released a ton of concept art for this  fight right here and as you can see we  do have doctor strange and wanda going  toe to toe now this would have been  quite the scene because as we know wanda  is pretty much just a pure raw magic raw  power user that is how she fights but  doctor strange is a little bit more  seasoned a little bit more skilled he's  not as powerful as wanda but he is a  little bit more knowledgeable about  magic now ultimately this scene would  have been sorcery versus witchcraft  which would have been some pretty dang  cool stuff to see however sadly they  went a different route for whatever  reason ultimately strange and america  chavez would be the only ones to go  through the portal and wanda would  remain at the carmitage and from there  she would torture poor wong and use the  darkhold to dreamwalk perhaps that  couldn't have happened if this scene  happened since wanda wasn't there  although she could have always just gone  back just the pure raw strength of  wanda's magic kind of makes it to where  she can pretty much do almost anything  she wants and if she wanted to go back  to the carmitage after traveling through  the multiverse it probably wouldn't have  been too hard however she would have  needed america chavez to somehow open up  a portal for her to get back and that's  where the problem lies and that is  probably why this scene was ultimately  scrapped however i do wish we would have  gotten a fight scene like this of wanda  going up against doctor strange  one-on-one toe-to-toe both in their  normal states not doctor strange as a  zombie i would have loved to see that  and i definitely think we were robbed  but hey let me know what you think about  these two deleted scenes that we didn't  get in multiverse of madness would you  have liked to have seen them and perhaps  maybe we will even get a nightmare scene  and a nightmare villain in a future  doctor strange movie but let me know  your thoughts in the comments down below  please don't forget to like the video  and subscribe so you don't miss out on  any of the latest mcu news for live  updates you can follow me on instagram  and twitter and as always thank you all  so much for watching woof

